39208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438360} {:answer/id #uuid "d95548b2-40ec-5ebf-b1ab-d29936ab04f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438360} :answer-field/id #uuid "168eb318-5e34-58b3-8153-3564c073e9ff" :answer-field/key "$x=5\\pi $ is in the domain of the function." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69d68c82-75d2-569e-bc5a-a35be8a71a62" :question/math-academy-id "q-65308" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement “The range of the function is all real numbers” is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=1,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$ is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $5\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement “$x=5\\pi $ is in the domain of the function” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050359 :topic/id #uuid "424e5d7e-179f-525e-bdaa-70125807f572" :topic/math-academy-id 3563 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e69034ac-dafa-5930-9534-071e532133a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451489} {:answer/id #uuid "c79d71f8-411a-5d53-9c3b-a808ff276fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e69034ac-dafa-5930-9534-071e532133a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451489} :answer-field/id #uuid "af683c1c-fb93-51f7-8ac5-a2a162727948" :answer-field/key "$x=-\\pi $ is not in the domain of the function." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aefb0cc-b61a-591b-938a-61ea84ad8322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451491} {:answer/id #uuid "94538785-9bb8-5d4c-adcd-8998ecf59214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aefb0cc-b61a-591b-938a-61ea84ad8322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451491} :answer-field/id #uuid "140a5ba5-395f-5a59-8c85-ed4334f12df7" :answer-field/key "$y=-\\frac{1}{3}$ is in the range of the function." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452593} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb55f19f-2e84-5c66-b274-dd496fc42c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451493} {:answer/id #uuid "e78d352f-70a9-5fb3-9cb7-e1d6d348d4bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e78d352f-70a9-5fb3-9cb7-e1d6d348d4bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451494} :answer-field/id #uuid "e01f97a5-285a-5298-bb3d-ba1bb2236b16" :answer-field/key "$x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e763b192-f670-5ee9-881f-7ff2a2620e1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-65332" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=sec⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](images/da/da729794a0331383debd75be0a4ce4a9f2d4da3286f50bd4f284868996077412.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “$x=-\\pi $ is not in the domain of the function” is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ thus it is defined for $x=-\\pi .$\n\n- Statement “$y=-\\frac{1}{3}$ is in the range of the function” is false. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=-\\frac{1}{3}$ is not in the range.\n\n- Statement “$x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote” is true. The function $y=sec⁡x$ has vertical asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $, thus $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050064 :topic/id #uuid "2a546664-10ba-55b4-ae58-ccb5dd16dca0" :topic/math-academy-id 1483 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Sine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70a785c2-393a-5a94-bf91-ca5ecd6971b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467722} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba108ea-f332-5102-ab91-06fceec4d251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70a785c2-393a-5a94-bf91-ca5ecd6971b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467722} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0d3662e-e09c-5f64-98c3-e20f9b22d088" :answer-field/key "$(0,-2\\pi )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9529cf39-39ef-5312-a424-5a724c472342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467724} {:answer/id #uuid "bb84cc54-6743-5846-8d91-94b5fc81de0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb84cc54-6743-5846-8d91-94b5fc81de0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467725} :answer-field/id #uuid "211c78a3-c7f3-5811-864c-a8d524c6218e" :answer-field/key "$(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "269da86c-2941-58e2-a59d-268c780b46cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467726} {:answer/id #uuid "204e2406-d430-5f85-b6af-e843171fc96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "204e2406-d430-5f85-b6af-e843171fc96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467727} :answer-field/id #uuid "36b3e117-4a2a-5afd-8320-ffa1d5324c25" :answer-field/key "$(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a75bb764-05ea-55ac-922e-cca49efb6283" :question/math-academy-id "q-65821" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(0,-2\\pi ).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-2\\pi ,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=-2\\pi $ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,-2\\pi )$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{1}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{4},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050064 :topic/id #uuid "2a546664-10ba-55b4-ae58-ccb5dd16dca0" :topic/math-academy-id 1483 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Sine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac8f2dda-cd81-5f6e-b768-a55c41ebc669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" 