question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4a752d35-73b8-55ea-bb50-4d11f60be65b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70669" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](images/8b/8bc549c68a3bc5b7989ac1835e4bb58183066c7797264b8cccd4f3fd2c895056.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function has no minimum value” is true. The function has no minimum or maximum value.\n\n- Statement “$x=-4\\pi $ is in the domain of the function” is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $n\\pi $ for any integer $n$, thus it is not defined for $x=-4\\pi .$\n\n- Statement “$x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function” is true. The zeros of $y=cot⁡x$ occur at $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n.$ Therefore, $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050064 :topic/id #uuid "2a546664-10ba-55b4-ae58-ccb5dd16dca0" :topic/math-academy-id 1483 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Sine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "619a4c51-2e05-537d-92f8-05b27adc0576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467812} {:answer/id #uuid "b91d959d-53f8-55db-a51e-4ff6ad7ddc62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "619a4c51-2e05-537d-92f8-05b27adc0576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467812} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fdac921-475b-5331-a99d-ec7b6d2ed4c0" :answer-field/key "$(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468627} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f35e836d-9bb8-578a-a543-2f4893a1ac7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467814} {:answer/id #uuid "bb49ae2b-5562-5a17-b362-7dd84e0030a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb49ae2b-5562-5a17-b362-7dd84e0030a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467815} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfdd3471-0795-5b0b-9ab3-357659c59d0f" :answer-field/key "$(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468628} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7240a062-fdde-5f4a-b323-b6fe3a7554d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467816} {:answer/id #uuid "0d23fd2f-ce53-5110-991d-3c8e82483cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7240a062-fdde-5f4a-b323-b6fe3a7554d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467816} :answer-field/id #uuid "67a4358a-90d6-55fb-8b57-f1e67df2bf37" :answer-field/key "$(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cc9d880f-4b58-5f10-97af-057cfca9838a" :question/math-academy-id "q-70714" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points.  \n\n- First, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$  does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$  does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110575 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af0b18ca-54a2-5a24-a670-faa311096abc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Cosine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048794 :topic/id #uuid "bf6b1d4a-a2a5-5f59-9697-5ed210454e3e" :topic/math-academy-id 1486 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Cosine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10156616-a9f7-5c47-aa77-4797186d49b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467818} {:answer/id #uuid "27d415f8-955c-56ec-94a5-840b1e90a20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10156616-a9f7-5c47-aa77-4797186d49b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467818} :answer-field/id #uuid "68d821be-63a7-5cf5-a99e-8be61ac0ed52" :answer-field/key "$(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468630} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aa5d04f-2f47-582d-9132-431e10289dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467820} {:answer/id #uuid "aef971cd-c6e8-5f8c-8ac7-feaea30c2119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aef971cd-c6e8-5f8c-8ac7-feaea30c2119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467821} :answer-field/id #uuid "609358db-d2ee-5d20-99a4-827822ea1fca" :answer-field/key "$(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{4})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468631} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cf00b7b-e193-5cf9-b0d6-13941f33188a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467822} {:answer/id #uuid "525d7fb9-cf7b-5db7-a1ab-7bcd832002e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "525d7fb9-cf7b-5db7-a1ab-7bcd832002e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467823} :answer-field/id #uuid "94979de1-58b5-53c5-8b92-d163dec29f80" :answer-field/key "$(-1,\\pi )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5a1259cd-784d-5b09-bc57-e1c65f1d431f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70768" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [0,\\pi ].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{1}{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{3\\pi }{4},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-1,\\pi ).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\pi ,-1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=\\pi $ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-1,\\pi )$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110575 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af0b18ca-54a2-5a24-a670-faa311096abc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Cosine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048794 :topic/id #uuid "bf6b1d4a-a2a5-5f59-9697-5ed210454e3e" :topic/math-academy-id 1486 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Cosine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0764b808-2439-5977-abc9-4df3e6e27d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467824} {:answer/id #uuid "1106e80c-03ae-5a78-95c0-228a6df04897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0764b808-2439-5977-abc9-4df3e6e27d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467824} :answer-