lty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7b495bf5-5746-5288-a51e-cecce774eb37" :question/math-academy-id "q-70770" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [0,\\pi ].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(-\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},-\\frac{1}{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{1}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range.   $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{5\\pi }{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110587 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b834b64-9679-56c2-b5e9-ee26a54b5e13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Values in the Domain of the Inverse Tangent Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049656 :topic/id #uuid "08bc988d-9fd4-51b9-b9a1-01573e3679f4" :topic/math-academy-id 1487 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Tangent Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a2d9a9-577b-5444-9d1c-92bf0a7facff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467830} {:answer/id #uuid "1eb1cc8e-f502-5f32-9bac-9ac87104593e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eb1cc8e-f502-5f32-9bac-9ac87104593e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467831} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dc6e9d1-002a-50a3-a1d6-0ec8dcb2822d" :answer-field/key "The number $-100$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468636} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ac0f876-2044-5dca-a2b2-310d5490c170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467832} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b6825a-d045-54b6-8a0f-5d3a523bf157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9b6825a-d045-54b6-8a0f-5d3a523bf157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467833} :answer-field/id #uuid "445a3cf5-5731-5612-b607-3b6bb49aa1ad" :answer-field/key "The number $-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7a23d11-138e-5745-91a2-f07870b98ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467834} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8c67de-3774-5868-85f9-8b1d22704542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b8c67de-3774-5868-85f9-8b1d22704542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467835} :answer-field/id #uuid "654e5696-0872-5218-a141-abbe7f718f40" :answer-field/key "The number $1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a65633b2-f520-54e4-8125-2639c369820d" :question/math-academy-id "q-70778" :question/problem "Which of the following values lies in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/68/6860bcf04c508b0abe795b9e1699163ac9495818f6427b338ac6bbe17774b2d8.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, all the given values are in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9110c50a-62db-5447-b4d0-60819c80eb31" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties Related to Point Discontinuities Given a Function Expression" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048614 :topic/id #uuid "aedeae90-38bd-5345-9896-abb52aad6dc6" :topic/math-academy-id 2002 :topic/title "Point Discontinuities"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd64c57e-db4c-58c2-9c0a-6fb1e52a8dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467836} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8068b5-f3a3-5dc6-a0ec-cecb527ccb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d8068b5-f3a3-5dc6-a0ec-cecb527ccb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467837} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2422695-230f-5927-9490-102b7e7aad51" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}g(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8baeab37-9b1a-57ad-b7b9-83f94da0b272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467838} {:answer/id #uuid "38e2dab8-9fb9-5e67-a816-3499bc06a78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8baeab37-9b1a-57ad-b7b9-83f94da0b272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467838} :answer-field/id #uuid "7db0f81d-fea3-51ed-b360-51d8b22165a7" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to 4}g(x)=g(4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468640} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a5f7ff8-b409-5399-af3b-b0798c72be3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467840} {:answer/id #uuid "9c5a5569-d89a-528c-8eda-f01b3b4a0dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c5a5569-d89a-528c-8eda-f01b3b4a0dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467841} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f8893a-0805-523d-a0fc-3f3104e0d117" :answer-field/key "$g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468641}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d44ff842-4620-550a-bab6-87cb0a1ac002" :question/math-academy-id "q-71179" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}3x, & x\\ne 4 \\\\ 13, & x=4,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our continuity conditions:\n\n- $g(4)=13$ exists$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{4}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{4}^{-}}3x=12, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{4}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{4}^{+}}3x=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude that statement ${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}g(x)$ is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 4}g(x)=12.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The value of the limit is ${lim}_{x\\to 4}g(x)=12,$ while the value of the function is $g(4)=13.$ So, statement ${lim}_{x\\to 4}g(x)=g(4)$ is false and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 4}g(x)\\ne g(4)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSince the third condition failed, the function has a removable discontinuity at $x=4,$ and statement “$g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=4$” is true.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements ${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}g(x)$ and “$g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=4$” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9110c50a-62db-5447-b4d0-60819c80eb31" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties Related to Point Discontinuities Given a Function Expression" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048614 :topic/id #uuid "aedeae90-38bd-5345-9896-abb52aad6dc6" :topic/math-academy-id 2002 :topic/title "Point Discontinuities"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33320f01-0cd9-5584-907b-111c2b4618bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451501} {:answer/id #uuid "f0914a41-9926-57c2-b640-64e281ead5b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0914a41-9926-57c2-b640-64e281ead5b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451502} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c990e01-c40c-5da0-8fc4-0a6f039e9d0a" :answer-field/key "$f(2)$ exists" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452598} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da9719ef-4224-52d2-9b65-6f8a550d673b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451503} {:answer/id #uuid "af90cee8-740f-5bac-a3e9-97fe948acd5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da9719ef-4224-52d2-9b65-6f8a550d673b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451503} :answer-field/id #uuid "4df650f8-a145-5f16-bbc5-ce42f328ee7e" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452599} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10f11098-ffae-5d4e-8926-4d749bc054bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451505} {:answer/id #uuid "7e11fba0-bfb2-52ec-a2c1-58f682f5fb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10f11098-ffae-5d4e-8926-4d749bc054bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451505} :answer-field/id #uuid "77d5729b-417b-567c-afdd-26291eaeb1dc" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b1ad50f-eeb7-5cca-b60f-fb6418344feb" :question/math-academy-id "q-71180" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}4x, & x<2 \\\\ 4, & x=2 \\\\ {x}^{2}, & x>2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements is true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our continuity conditions:\n\n- $f(2)=4$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, statement “$f(2)$ exists” is true.\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}(4x)=8, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}{x}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that statement ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)$ is false and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x).\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSince the second condition failed, $x=2$ is not a removable discontinuity. So, statement “$f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=2$” is false.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement “$f(2)$ exists” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049882 :topic/id #uuid "1ad374f3-e4f4-5dcc-ab6d-d6aed0790f3a" :topic/math-academy-id 1900 :topic/title "Level Curves"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97b5337a-3e06-5fca-8dee-9ccb9bb3e791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467842} {:answer/id #uuid "ca10f725-532e-52f8-b216-80660df1aff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97b5337a-3e06-5fca-8dee-9ccb9bb3e791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467842} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f26b394-09a9-58cd-8127-d23fbca6af8c" :answer-field/key "$c=3$ gives a hyperbola" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468642} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "572c0f09-8cda-57e4-84ee-e9bf11b0969a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467844} {:answer/id #uuid "3debfd10-6252-58a8-80d0-0fe4ad6b3d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3debfd10-6252-58a8-80d0-0fe4ad6b3d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467845} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4b044d1-ec5c-5118-ba8c-99f2a5e9c147" :answer-field/key "$c=0$ gives an ellipse" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468643} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d92d5ae0-bdbf-5aac-a192-d4634abd4820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467846} {:answer/id #uuid "80aced54-71e3-53cc-8d38-ae55e211374c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80aced54-71e3-53cc-8d38-ae55e211374c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467847} :answer-field/id #uuid "7551102b-2721-527c-a9e6-1c6948d2bf34" :answer-field/key "$c=1$ gives a circle" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e04ff7ee-ed94-5861-b7e8-a3f79254490c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71391" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4}{{y}^{2}}$, clear the denominator in $f(x,y)=c$ and classify the resulting conic equation in the entire $xy$-plane, including points excluded from the function's domain. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4}{{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4 & =c{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(3-c){y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curves are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{2},$ which consists of two vertical lines.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=4,$ which is an ellipse.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2,$ which is a circle.\n\nSo, only statements “$c=0$ gives an ellipse” and “$c=1$ gives a circle” are true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049882 :topic/id #uuid "1ad374f3-e4f4-5dcc-ab6d-d6aed0790f3a" :topic/math-academy-id 1900 :topic/title "Level Curves"} :activity/title "Level Curves" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529572} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530562}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049882 :topic/id #uuid "1ad374f3-e4f4-5dcc-ab6d-d6aed0790f3a" :topic/math-academy-id 1900 :topic/title "Level Curves"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a0a2c4b-1d93-5837-bae6-4a3c28e16089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467848} {:answer/id #uuid "14a75206-caba-527a-ab7a-6a2b9a8d8748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a0a2c4b-1d93-5837-bae6-4a3c28e16089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467848} :answer-field/id #uuid "19c95e90-566c-5c73-bd5c-bb5cbff441a5" :answer-field/key "$c=1$ gives a line" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468645} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb7223c5-838d-5ef7-859b-ec117f5a0b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467850} {:answer/id #uuid "83112c20-89a5-5790-800e-3e3c93383a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83112c20-89a5-5790-800e-3e3c93383a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467851} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd2bacc0-d212-57b2-89ee-6c74f13e09de" :answer-field/key "$c=2$ gives a hyperbola" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468646} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c053cde-7b3e-5844-88a1-fbf51c0cc806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467852} {:answer/id #uuid "0514df20-5bca-51ca-8efc-b76c2c3044a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0514df20-5bca-51ca-8efc-b76c2c3044a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467853} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a2ff425-5344-55a6-a715-3662f57b95c1" :answer-field/key "$c=0$ gives two lines" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b94a6f8a-60a9-5806-9e18-4814d39c5835" :question/math-academy-id "q-71395" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=1,$ which is not a line.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=4,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}},$ which consists of two lines.\n\nSo, only statements “$c=2$ gives a hyperbola” and “$c=0$ gives two lines” are true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049882 :topic/id #uuid "1ad374f3-e4f4-5dcc-ab6d-d6aed0790f3a" :topic/math-academy-id 1900 :topic/title "Level Curves"} :activity/title "Level Curves" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421485} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421496}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08a9d9fb-59ba-5f9e-9ed4-0dd4dd47d776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451513} {:answer/id #uuid "3353c7cf-f540-50b8-b410-f9464bae62df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08a9d9fb-59ba-5f9e-9ed4-0dd4dd47d776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451513} :answer-field/id #uuid "105aa68e-efe5-5792-a05e-ab62905759d4" :answer-field/key "The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,5,2⟩.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e37b877f-2a3f-5fed-9ad8-fb2c168a8f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451515} {:answer/id #uuid "5aebbcaf-2c44-5bbd-8d57-983ab8f1a5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5aebbcaf-2c44-5bbd-8d57-983ab8f1a5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451516} :answer-field/id #uuid "76c3952f-a2e7-5826-84ff-a1d6a0428f2c" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452605} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a50e1758-2a18-5eda-97ec-ee302f243927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451517} {:answer/id #uuid "624bf4db-24cc-5399-8313-772b1909a576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a50e1758-2a18-5eda-97ec-ee302f243927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451517} :answer-field/id #uuid "31fa76a4-c8ce-5442-94a2-8831eb85b68a" :answer-field/key "The planes are coincident." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59fa73e3-7e11-58b8-85f9-3fcdbce086ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-71456" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-3y+z=0$ and $2x-y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-3y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-3,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x-y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,-1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,5,2⟩.$” is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+2j+5k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,5⟩\\ne ⟨1,5,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement “The planes are coincident” is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes cannot be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e2afd41-011d-50b7-bdd6-b2fe0e79319a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451519} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a8a6a1-4d09-5b9a-87bf-b8affe56cc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e2afd41-011d-50b7-bdd6-b2fe0e79319a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451519} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4ff5205-ba68-5bf5-9b0a-caec3fa1d55c" :answer-field/key "The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,6,-5⟩.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4573706-4ddd-5c59-ae75-f76209f442b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451521} {:answer/id #uuid "8a64a65e-cbd5-5aa2-9fc1-b39766e3b1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4573706-4ddd-5c59-ae75-f76209f442b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451521} :answer-field/id #uuid "a02ea405-f5ad-5f66-b8b5-c7c965e15944" :answer-field/key "The planes are parallel." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452608} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e1367f-c77e-5db8-87a9-df2724a72ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451523} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf169b7-e727-58e0-a834-1eca473c044e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdf169b7-e727-58e0-a834-1eca473c044e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451524} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ecb6f3e-52a7-56a2-9a87-95a8d2a508e8" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "894f2787-9676-52de-a718-3b82f8fd7a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71463" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x+3y+2z=0$ and $x-y-z=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x+3y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,3,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y-z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,6,-5⟩.$” is false. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,3,2⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+5j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-6⟩\\ne ⟨1,6,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The planes are parallel” is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the corresponding planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"} :activity/title "The Intersection of Two Planes" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421888} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421905}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ef64022-0288-5e76-8bb0-1ca193d77eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451525} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfde92f-2266-5a57-a77b-9186eb8b35e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdfde92f-2266-5a57-a77b-9186eb8b35e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451526} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbec3c98-7285-563e-ab93-4e996e9fbaae" :answer-field/key "The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,-2,-2⟩.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452610} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64e99a15-12e3-5f98-8c02-7a61a29e41e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451527} {:answer/id #uuid "1afa0967-d19f-5ead-9712-05b4c3746b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64e99a15-12e3-5f98-8c02-7a61a29e41e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451527} :answer-field/id #uuid "193f4082-ae02-52c1-a2e0-34b89151c4b4" :answer-field/key "The normal vectors of the planes are parallel." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6bda1b9-d22e-5990-a8f9-5869cb11938f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451529} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e169a5-4cbe-5477-b7e2-f3cb319f9ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2e169a5-4cbe-5477-b7e2-f3cb319f9ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451530} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0b3bf2b-8f9f-51d2-b5f4-e6f63de89d4f" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55226586-d156-5c41-9a9d-ff9a0c5b3e34" :question/math-academy-id "q-71464" :question/problem "Given the two planes $y-z=1$ and $2x+z=3$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $y-z=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,-1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+z=3,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,-2,-2⟩.$” is true. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨0,1,-1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i-2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The normal vectors of the planes are parallel” is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a line” is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statements “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,-2,-2⟩.$” and  “The planes intersect on a line” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050991 :topic/id #uuid "7789d7fa-bfec-58c3-afd1-afcff30a8748" :topic/math-academy-id 2539 :topic/title "The Intersection of Two Planes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96dfc723-c739-5f3e-8f21-0b626c09e1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451531} {:answer/id #uuid "97b76965-dd4a-52ed-930f-e1d960bbf66b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97b76965-dd4a-52ed-930f-e1d960bbf66b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74be5fe-bbae-51b8-be42-776a486c8913" :answer-field/key "The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "819e2d79-747a-537e-b412-468c4ceadea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451533} {:answer/id #uuid "036ccda4-6962-5c5a-82b9-fcd5b6624f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "819e2d79-747a-537e-b412-468c4ceadea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451533} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c2940e9-01bd-5899-9120-b872a698e75e" :answer-field/key "The planes intersect on a straight line." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "564ac206-0781-50cf-81c9-0e7b9d70d384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451535} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ad7deb-c245-5226-b91a-5ea92b19e6e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "564ac206-0781-50cf-81c9-0e7b9d70d384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451535} :answer-field/id #uuid "9551997d-c399-5b54-b209-0e56d0ead71f" :answer-field/key "The planes are coincident." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb6d9712-df0c-5f4b-a820-ccc73d9a1ec9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71468" :question/problem "Given the two planes $2x-4y+6z+2=0$ and $-x+2y-3z=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $2x-4y+6z+2=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-4,6⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $-x+2y-3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨-1,2,-3⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$” is true. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨2,-4,6⟩\\times ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =0i+0j+0k \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The planes intersect on a straight line” is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}=0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes are also parallel. So, the planes can't intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement “The planes are coincident” is false. Indeed,  the second plane passes through the origin  $O(0,0,0)$ but the first plane doesn't: \n\n$$\n2(0)-4(0)+6(0)+2=2\\ne 0\n$$\n\n So, the planes can't be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d01f57d9-5382-51fc-bab4-ffea738f1ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467854} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b404fe-5087-57bf-b263-c61589eb6cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d01f57d9-5382-51fc-bab4-ffea738f1ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467854} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e01aee-b504-51ec-a835-86adeb5908ec" :answer-field/key "$(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468648} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7303305-82d7-590b-bd4e-1a4e70d19cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467856} {:answer/id #uuid "95ef83b9-f720-5a51-bbca-96fc09dbbf9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95ef83b9-f720-5a51-bbca-96fc09dbbf9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467857} :answer-field/id #uuid "bac3a257-72fb-5727-a2e2-607cc6489f5b" :answer-field/key "$[-1,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468649} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68c2fa7d-c1fb-55e0-9e76-3d220bf461d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467858} {:answer/id #uuid "1e4ddb26-d234-57e3-82d0-9980a51f2163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68c2fa7d-c1fb-55e0-9e76-3d220bf461d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467858} :answer-field/id #uuid "37d88f0f-e223-519e-a68d-b17bad084659" :answer-field/key "$(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1e22680-b6e5-5705-939d-f4a384a3db7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71791" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[-1,1]$ is closed. The boundary points are $-1$, and $1.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$ has a boundary point $3$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$ has a boundary point $0$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $[-1,1]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15e435d9-0d0c-57a7-b750-2fe6e91de38a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467860} {:answer/id #uuid "124179ee-ec18-565c-8e41-d6a38b6648d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "124179ee-ec18-565c-8e41-d6a38b6648d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467861} :answer-field/id #uuid "d32fbe7a-e8bf-58e8-87a2-4469f95dadcb" :answer-field/key "$(-\\infty ,-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468651} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b04679a-cdc2-503e-9e56-5f54340d850e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467862} {:answer/id #uuid "560bd919-6c05-51e5-be0a-1e97bf0f2100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b04679a-cdc2-503e-9e56-5f54340d850e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467862} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f59797d-12b2-53fc-b302-f28e7b141f34" :answer-field/key "$(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468652} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4bc2964-0554-5078-acf3-fb9a8ebdd1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467864} {:answer/id #uuid "d53b6194-061b-5e9a-bb9a-e89015f4c765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4bc2964-0554-5078-acf3-fb9a8ebdd1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467864} :answer-field/id #uuid "95be5ba9-d56c-5766-a506-02a900406ee5" :answer-field/key "$[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20e43566-ea3c-59ee-a80b-84f1522c9eea" :question/math-academy-id "q-71798" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-\\infty ,-2)$ is open. The boundary point of the set is $-2$ and it does not lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$ has four boundary points $0$, $2$, $7$, and $9$, and the points $2$, $7$, and $9$ lies in the set.\n\n- $[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$ has four boundary points $-5$, $-1$, $2$, and $4$, and the points $-5$ and $-1$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(-\\infty ,-2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d97f9b1-cd02-5db7-b2bc-f5cc82fd1fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467866} {:answer/id #uuid "16d6c84b-080a-524c-9f25-2308e8f31793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d97f9b1-cd02-5db7-b2bc-f5cc82fd1fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467866} :answer-field/id #uuid "262aa83b-bc34-5f27-a72e-d2195e3fc4a0" :answer-field/key "$[-7,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d94692c-4b2e-5