ts only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-5,-1)$ is open. The boundary points are $-5$, and $-1.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $[-7,1]$ has two boundary points $-7$, and $1$, and both of them lie in the set.\n\n- $(-1,3]\\cup [4,5)$ has four boundary points $-1$, $3$, $4$, and $5$, and the points $3$ and $4$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(-5,-1)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0facf7b-b440-550d-a4f0-7ff4c1c70086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467872} {:answer/id #uuid "923dab7f-47a4-5a3e-98eb-2cce0c04c4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "923dab7f-47a4-5a3e-98eb-2cce0c04c4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467873} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b347d78-d76c-546b-9764-685fc8bce910" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }x<y<{x}^{2},\\\\\\,1<x\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468657} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22a04b7c-fb3d-5af9-ac13-b910623c1d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467874} {:answer/id #uuid "22c1d005-4f0b-5972-a387-b7ee798fd110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22a04b7c-fb3d-5af9-ac13-b910623c1d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467874} :answer-field/id #uuid "6202c391-be1c-57b1-848b-195b5e71c27f" :answer-field/key "$\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }2<y<x\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5074ee4-5219-56ad-b17c-122d6139dd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467876} {:answer/id #uuid "8b927c21-a2f7-54c8-a565-a983c6bbb42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b927c21-a2f7-54c8-a565-a983c6bbb42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467877} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c56bb76-335e-5a28-aec0-4d8270bf15ec" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }4\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<9\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1615097-eb1e-5984-b134-50e4277f6126" :question/math-academy-id "q-71814" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,2).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }x<y<{x}^{2},\\\\\\,1<x\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }4\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<9\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338994 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b5c97d8-b6b9-59d5-9e48-f02e00576bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "