atrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$  is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048980 :topic/id #uuid "d0f342d9-c70c-537f-9e04-f3b0beaf9c01" :topic/math-academy-id 2083 :topic/title "Row Echelon Form"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7311cb50-f585-5f8b-8c7c-43ea3935ca30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467950} {:answer/id #uuid "5df8e8f3-9308-5944-af31-4d14c71a9d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7311cb50-f585-5f8b-8c7c-43