ent :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "468e9b34-a780-5fca-a56d-a2a2883f4d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467960} {:answer/id #uuid "a0aec6ac-9ba7-5c44-9c4a-8f2c4061212f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "468e9b34-a780-5fca-a56d-a2a2883f4d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467960} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a4e593-82f4-562c-a9f7-3bfab9eb0154" :answer-field/key "$C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c409d434-4c7f-59fa-9d55-4c82bc621cc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-72574" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied). \n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}6 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & 7 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048980 :topic/id #uuid "d0f342d9-c70c-537f-9e04-f3b0beaf9c01" :topic/math-academy-id 2083 :topic/title "Row Echelon Form"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60637292-3e09-530b-ac61-fcbbce897d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467962} {:answer/id #uuid "e4dad7c2-9a72-5985-95d5-14eb19840971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60637292-3e09-530b-ac61-fcbbce897d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467962} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf03a675-2bed-5618-b8f1-977c4c5732ba" :answer-field/key "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468702} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8421492d-9fc4-581e-9662-4c6ad1d30585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467964} {:answer/id #uuid "57892105-0d46-58cf-b489-d7654d7df5df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57892105-0d46-58cf-b489-d7654d7df5df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467965} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac1b36ea-8d6f-51c9-bc43-9c783cb2e595" :answer-field/key "$B=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75ae5575-30a3-527c-957b-e31d7bd513e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467966} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c77217-c4e4-5860-8c50-aec83eb153e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75ae5575-30a3-527c-957b-e31d7bd513e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467966} :answer-field/id #uuid "0477e48c-0ee5-5ea3-a796-a287db3e0107" :answer-field/key "$C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2d3c090e-cc4f-51d5-a663-f597f7113489" :question/math-academy-id "q-72576" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341908 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050657 :topic/id #uuid "5cf444d7-d014-59c7-b47c-21b442662b58" :topic/math-academy-id 474 :topic/title "Left and Right Continuity"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fb1b728-e5c1-56d0-a773-6a13b86c144a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467968} {:answer/id #uuid "1f3e086a-3eee-5014-bba7-217442e99470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fb1b728-e5c1-56d0-a773-6a13b86c144a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467968} :answer-field/id #uuid "5010ced0-6c65-57ca-86ab-3156cee7409a" :answer-field/key "The function is left-continuous at $x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468705} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b93087-ad7b-53c4-b3da-e44b9829803b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467970} {:answer/id #uuid "e772286c-b6b9-5b76-afdf-c7a1d919f850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e772286c-b6b9-5b76-afdf-c7a1d919f850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467971} :answer-field/id #uuid "59560ccb-ca91-5b45-807c-a046f0c20497" :answer-field/key "The function is right-continuous at $x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "068e637a-e3be-5f92-a484-ea2d9e3dc524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467972} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ebd06a-49a6-522d-8839-e499931d4990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "068e637a-e3be-5f92-a484-ea2d9e3dc524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467972} :answer-field/id #uuid "e764c6f9-b95b-5630-b381-cb9920f27ccc" :answer-field/key "The function is continuous at $x=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79464211-37d1-5cac-b164-284bb9d9308a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73105" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad3fb8a0cce2a6dac706d7876aca0a2339fe49c05cb7aa6ae54de86735ceafab.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “The function is left-continuous at $x=3$” is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=3,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x)=3\\ne 1=f(3)\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function is right-continuous at $x=3$” is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=3,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}f(x)=1=f(3)\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function is continuous at $x=3$” is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=3,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement “The function is right-continuous at $x=3$” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050657 :topic/id #uuid "5cf444d7-d014-59c7-b47c-21b442662b58" :topic/math-academy-id 474 :topic/title "Left and Right Continuity"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a608917-3bf1-55b6-a1bb-215006677c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} 